From d90ab9e94f63cac9167238c6356552bf725fa0ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aker1305 <aker1305@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:44:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Speak announcements from the background timer service

With the screen locked or the app in the background the UI does not
rebuild, so announcements triggered from the run screen were silent.

- Vendor background_hiit_timer 1.2.3 (MIT, same author) under
  packages/ and speak from its service isolate, where the timer sounds
  already play
- The app writes the texts for the current workout to SharedPreferences
  (voiceAnnouncementTexts); the service speaks them on interval change
- Remove the UI-side announcer

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5W6dQ9ZgyihWUfbUDrb4L
